// Every card's sounds (SPEC §10.11, R655). apps/web/src/audio/voiceData.ts reads this file when the
// client loads and apps/web/scripts/gen-voice.mjs renders its voice lines. Nothing writes it back, so
// comments and trailing commas are safe. A mistake fails the load and the tests, naming its path.
//
// Four sections, in this order:
//   voices   the voices a line can be spoken in, by name in alphabetical order. A macOS `say` voice
//            gives say, rate (90-360), pbas and pmod (0-127); backend: "sapi" is a Windows SAPI one
//            instead, with voice, rate (-50-100), semitones (-12-12) and an ffmpeg filter chain. web
//            is the browser's fallback pitch (0-2) and rate (0.1-10), gain a trim on the rendered
//            files (0-2).
//   effects  the sound effects a card can play. sfx names one of the procedural recipes in sfx.ts
//            (SFX_IDS); pitch shifts it (1 as written, 0.5 an octave down, 2 an octave up, 0.25-4),
//            gain trims it (0-2), and params passes the recipe its own options (amount, timbre,
//            mine, mythic, urgent, release). Each play varies the pitch a little.
//   cards    one entry per catalog card, in catalog order, with the card's name in a comment on
//            the line of its id. The name is for people; a test checks it against the catalog.
//   emotes   the six hero portraits' emote lines (R644), one entry per portrait id, each a voice
//            from the voices bank and its five lines: greetings, wellPlayed, oops, thanks, threaten.
//
// A card's hooks are when its sounds play:
//   play     a Unit played, or put onto the field by an effect
//   attack   a Unit of yours picked up to attack (dragged, or clicked to choose its target)
//   death    a Unit destroyed
//   cast     a Spell or Field Spell cast, a Trap or Field Trap firing
// A hook gives a voice line, { voice: "<a voice>", text: "<the line>" }, an effect,
// { effect: "<an effect>" }, or both in one object; with both, the effect starts first.
//
// To add a card: copy a neighbour's entry to where the catalog puts the card, change the id and the
// name comment, and give a Unit a play and a death line, anything else a cast line. A new or changed
// line has to be rendered: `pnpm --filter @jackioh/web gen:voice` on macOS, or on Windows (or WSL)
// for a SAPI voice. Effects render nothing.
{
  voices: {
    alien: { say: "Trinoids", rate: 170, pbas: 45, pmod: 20, web: { pitch: 0.5, rate: 0.9 }, gain: 1.66 },
    // Ceaseless Void's own pitch and pace.
    "alien-void": { say: "Trinoids", rate: 150, pbas: 25, pmod: 20, web: { pitch: 0.5, rate: 0.9 }, gain: 1.66 },
    announcer: { say: "Superstar", rate: 190, pbas: 50, pmod: 50, web: { pitch: 1.2, rate: 1.1 } },
    brute: { say: "Fred", rate: 165, pbas: 28, pmod: 15, web: { pitch: 0.5, rate: 0.9 }, gain: 1.71 },
    // Chaos Golem's own pitch and pace.
